 ### D4. Retry transition
 
-`refreshing` on a transient error moves to `retrying` while fewer than two retries were made, else to `failed`. See D3 for the backoff delays.
+`refreshing` on a transient error moves to `retrying` while fewer than two retries were made, else to `failed`. The backoff delays are those of the spec requirement "Transient refresh failures are retried" (specs/session-refresh/spec.md). `refresh()` waits through an injected `sleep(ms)` that defaults to a `setTimeout` wrapper, so `test/refresh.test.ts` records the exact delays the delivered code requests without reading the wall clock.
 
 ## Verification
 
-F1 scenario 2 (shared in-flight refresh) keeps its outputs under `f1/scenario-2/`.
+Task 2.1 (F1) is the single source for F1 scenarios and evidence paths. F1 runs the delivered `src/refresh.ts` and `src/session.ts` unmodified; `tools/fake-idp.ts` replaces only the identity provider's token endpoint, because a real provider cannot be made to answer 503 or `invalid_grant` on demand. It sends the responses the client handles in production: HTTP 503, HTTP 400 with body `{"error":"invalid_grant"}` (RFC 6749 §5.2), and a token response. It issues synthetic tokens only; F1 reads and writes no real credential.
